# Marathon Librem 5 CPU governor override
#
# marathon-base-config ships 60-marathon-cpufreq.rules which sets
# `schedutil` on every CPU. On i.MX 8M Quad with mainline kernel,
# schedutil's PELT-based ramp is too slow for Marathon's startup load
# spike (shell + Wayland compositor + WebEngine + 30 services racing
# to D-Bus) — CPUs sit at 200-400 MHz when they should be at 1.5 GHz,
# producing the ~2 fps / 30 s touch latency the user reported on r11.
#
# Phosh works smoothly on the same hardware under schedutil because
# GTK + phoc is roughly 3× lighter than Qt6 + Marathon's Wayland
# compositor + WebEngine pre-warm. Marathon needs the headroom.
#
# udev rules fire in lexicographic order and RUN+= both runs — the
# LAST write to scaling_governor wins. 99- runs after 60-, so this
# leaves the governor at `performance`.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="cpu", KERNEL=="cpu[0-9]*", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'echo performance > /sys/devices/system/cpu/%k/cpufreq/scaling_governor'"
